<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vindonissa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vindonissa was a Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionary</a> fortress at present-day Windisch, in the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aargau">Aargau</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, near the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aare">Aare</a> and the Reuss. Founded around 15 CE, it housed legions guarding the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> until about 101, and in the late third and fourth centuries it was refortified against Alemannic raids. Its remains include an amphitheatre and parts of the walls and gates.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vindonissa.jpg" alt="Vindonissa" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vindonissa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
